    "created_at": "2020-01-31T22:02:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-31T22:02:39Z",
    "body": "I think `sync()` would be a good addition. I haven't yet run into a use case for it myself though, so I don't have any examples other than the ones you've already mentioned.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure about the name. I would have liked `flush()`, but that already has a meaning for transform streams. `yield()` could work, but that could get confusing with the `yield` keyword (although the same could be said of `Promise.catch()`, `Promise.finally()` and `Iterator.return()`). Anyway, this might just be me bikeshedding. 😅 ",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
